---Decorative component that simply draws an image onto the screen.
---
---This is mostly an extension of ui.SpriteData, with the only functionality besides what's provided by that and by
---`Component` being functionality to associate this component with an object, making it so the object's model is drawn
---instead of the normal component contents.
---
---Warning: These components don't currently support segmented sprites, with the `visualMargin` property getting
---ignored.
---@class ui.Sprite : ui.Component
---@field associatedObjectID integer Numeric ID for the object associated with this component, or -1 if no associated object exists.
---@field associatedObjectQuantity integer The quantity for the object associated with this component.
---@field associatedObjectQuantityMode ui.ObjectQuantityDisplayMode Specifies when the label listing the quantity for the associated object should be displayed.
---@field sprite integer|RuntimeSprite|PluginImageResource
---@field spriteID integer Gets the built-in sprite ID to draw.
---@field runtimeSprite RuntimeSprite? Gets the current runtime sprite to draw or nil if it doesn't exist.
---@field visualMargins ui.Margin (Modifiable Contents) Offsets used to split this sprite's graphics into multiple segments for drawing. In the client: It gives a copy: setting one of its sides changes nothing, so assign a whole margin, which works.
---@field outlineWidth integer Thickness of the sprite's outline. Only used when the containing component is associated with an object.
---@field rotationDegrees number Rotation of this sprite in degrees.
---@field rotationRadians number Rotation of this sprite in radians.
---@field isFlippedHorizontally boolean Flag indicating whether or not this sprite is drawn mirrored horizontally.
---@field isFlippedVertical boolean Flag indicating whether or not this sprite is drawn mirrored vertical.
---@field isTiling boolean Flag indicating whether or not this sprite uses tiled visuals.
---@field shadowColour Vector4 Colour used when drawing this sprite's shadow. If alpha is 0, no shadow will be drawn.
---@field shadowRGBA Long Hex-encoded red/green/blue/alpha colour code used when drawing this sprite. If alpha is 0, no shadow will be drawn.
ui.Sprite = {}

---Creates a new sprite component on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this sprite component in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.Sprite # The newly created sprite component. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.Sprite.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Associates an object with this component, making it use the object's name and optionally it's quantity as the
---displayed contents for this component.
---@param objectID integer Numeric ID for the object to associate with this component.
---@param quantity? Long The quantity for the object to associate with this component.
function ui.Sprite:SetAssociatedObject(objectID, quantity) end

---Sets this Sprite's properties based on the provided config values.
---@param config ui.SpriteDataConfig The config to source the various properties from.
function ui.Sprite:SetConfig(config) end

---Returns a copy of this Sprite's config, allowing it to be used elsewhere.
---@return ui.SpriteDataConfig # Config containing a copy of all properties set on this Sprite object, excluding non-config properties (eg. `content`)
function ui.Sprite:GetConfigCopy() end

---Enumeration identifying how the quantity of an associated object should be displayed on a sprite with an associated
---object.
---
---Info: The font used for the quantity indicator is currently hardcoded.
---@enum ui.ObjectQuantityDisplayMode
ui.ObjectQuantityDisplayMode = {
    ---The quantity indicator is never displayed.
    NEVER = 0,
    ---The quantity indicator is always displayed.
    ALWAYS = 1,
    ---The quantity indicator is displayed if there's more than one object in the stack.
    MULTIPLE = 2,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `ui.ObjectQuantityDisplayMode.FromID(ui.ObjectQuantityDisplayMode.NEVER)` is `"NEVER"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function ui.ObjectQuantityDisplayMode.FromID(value) end
